es we're out  there telling the story and that's you  know and they're doing that often  through social media channels and that's  a great way for the company to build its  visibility to build its brand and to  then get the end customers who are  actually purchasing the product  absolutely so starlet at softbank you  focus on gamification media digital  media ecommerce just name a few  gamification though is a buzzword and  the business community right now so I  was wondering if you can speak a little  bit about what we're seeing in terms of  retail and gamification or e-commerce  and gamification yes I think we've seen  it for a while now you know guilt was  built on the back of referrals and  membership in this concept of  exclusivity and there you know there  were loyalty programs there there were  things like having early access having  special access those are all  gamification tools and certainly it's  something that we encourage and we see  and and those are successful techniques  to to either engage the customers to get  them to purchase to get them to tell  other people to get more customers so  definitely a believer in gamification as  a way to accelerate the business of  these e-commerce companies you know I'll  give you a quick example guilt last week  did an exclusive partnership with Kim  kardashian-west for her new selfish book  that's actually not launching till next  month and they had this early preview  where there were 500 copies that were  autographed and individually numbered by  her she tweeted and posted about it the  day before I think there was something  like 800 thousand likes and posts or all  sorts of social engagements and when the  books went on sale the next day they  sold out in one minute right so she  built that anticipation there's a  scarcity factor there that is critical  and important really  acting the customers and sure enough you  know it's old instantly and then they  were actually a few other books that  sold the same day as well so you know  definitely feel that gamification is  really interesting technique I think  that the companies that have been the  smartest about doing it and what I like  better is when there's already been some  demonstration of some value that the  company's obtained before they give away  whatever it is so as an example you know  it's not until you've made three  purchases that you then get the right to  you know give something away or give a  referral or a free gift or something  like that so that you've already  recouped upfront some of that  acquisition costs through the prior  customer who already has engaged and  already spent some money yeah so I gave  the example of our runway which I think  with these photo reviews is there's a  form of gamification we've actually  found that often our consumer wants to  share and wants to give data and  information as like sometimes even more  when you don't give them an incentive or  reward so I think there's also been a  trend of like so many almost freebies or  incentive things that customers almost  like are a little skeptical about it and  sometimes just the sheer like desire to  share with the community or hey I looked  and felt great in this dress like makes  them want to share on their own which  has been wonderful for us another what I  guess you could call gamification tool  that we've seen a lot of success with is  called Rent the Runway pro um and allah  amazon prime it enables you for a flat  fee and ours is thirty dollars a year to  get free shipping and insurance on your  orders and then there's other perks like  you get a credit for your birthday and  you get to you know I think gift a  friend address and all of that so that  for us is driven loyalty in a huge way  and so I think just looking at what  other companies have done in the  gamification space i know we looked a  lot at what guilt had done as we thought  about our customer acquisition strategy  is a great a great tool these days and  amaz